---
name: "Plan Change"
description: "Plans the issue and writes plan artifacts"
tags: [plan]
stage: plan
---
Read the current issue first:

```bash
mo issue view ${{ issue.number }} --project ${{ issue.projectId }}
```

Research the repository under `REPOS/${{ repository.name }}` and write:

- `PLANS/PLAN.md`: scope, approach, risks, and acceptance interpretation.
- `PLANS/DESIGN.md`: technical decisions and rationale. Always create this file; state that no separate design is needed when applicable.
- `PLANS/tasks.json`: an ordered implementation task list with this exact shape:

```json
{"tasks":[{"id":"T-001","title":"...","goal":"...","acceptance":["..."],"refs":["PLANS/DESIGN.md#..."]}]}
```

Each task is a complete vertical increment including its tests. Use only `id`, `title`, `goal`, `acceptance`, and `refs`. Keep tasks ordered; do not add dependency, priority, mode, type, output, notes, uses, with, or expect fields.
